      <main>

                                 <article id="main-content" class="article main-content container-fluid" role="article">
          
                                                                <header class="row content-header">
                         <section id="block-entityviewcontent-14" data-block-plugin-id="entity_view:node" class="block block-ctools block-entity-viewnode clearfix">
  
    

      
<div class="col-sm-12 col-md-8 col-md-offset-2">

  <h1 class="content-title text-center">Drug Safety Communications</h1>
  	
</div>

  </section>






                      </header>
                              
                                                          
                              <aside class="col-md-2" role="complementary">
                  <section id="block-entityviewcontent-3" data-block-plugin-id="entity_view:node" class="block block-ctools block-entity-viewnode clearfix">
  
    

      
  <div class="region region-">
        <nav id="section-nav" class="lcds-card lcds-section-nav lcds-section-nav--side hidden-xs hidden-sm">
      <ul class="lcds-section-nav__list lcds-section-nav--side__list">

        <li>

          
          
                                                
                        
                     
                <a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/drug-safety-communications" class="lcds-section-nav__link lcds-section-nav--side__link lcds-section-nav__parent-link lcds-section-nav--side__parent-link">Drug Safety Communications</a>                
                          

                        <div class="views-element-container form-group"><div class="view view-in-this-section view-id-in_this_section view-display-id-block_4 js-view-dom-id-9cef69bdf9a7e83a7771aa80cdd6525e02bd53326b8d41b0484c1b1cdd65db50">
  
    
      
  
          </div>
</div>


                        <div class="views-element-container form-group"><div class="view view-in-this-section-sub view-id-in_this_section_sub view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-1b292610c40a195cc146f91407983fb9035ea7acfd6577e541dbaaad18875aa2">
  
    
      
  
          </div>
</div>


        </li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
    </div>

  </section>


                </aside>
              
                                                          
              <div class="col-md-8" role="main">

                            
                            
                            
                            
                                              
  <p class="text-align-center"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/comunicaciones-de-la-fda-sobre-la-seguridad-de-los-medicamentos-en-espanol"><span><span class="text">Español</span></span></a>&nbsp;<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/yaowuanquantongxun"><span><span class="text">药物安全通讯</span></span></a>&nbsp;<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/fda-drug-safety-podcasts"><span><span class="text">Drug Safety Podcasts</span></span></a></p><p>FDA Drug Safety Communications are intended to provide important information to patients and health care professionals about new safety issues with the medicines they are taking or prescribing so they can make more informed decisions about treatment.</p><p>Widespread or long-term use of drugs by patients may uncover side effects not discovered during the clinical trials a drug company did to get FDA approval of the medicine. &nbsp;As a result, FDA physicians and scientists continue to monitor the safety of drugs after they are approved. &nbsp;When we learn information about a potential new safety issue, we review the data from available clinical trials or other studies, case reports, and medical literature. &nbsp;Based on what we find, we may require changes to the prescribing information or the patient Medication Guide. We may also release a Drug Safety Communication to alert patients and health care professionals about the issue. <a href="/drugs/surveillance-post-drug-approval-activities/postmarketing-surveillance-programs" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="7c1186cb-4ffa-4494-8eac-ecbf5b7c455a" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Postmarketing Surveillance Programs">Read more</a>.</p><p>You can get new safety information on medicines you’re prescribing or taking by signing up for <a href="https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/subscriber/new">email alerts</a> about Drug Safety Communications on types of drugs or medical specialties of specific interest to you.</p><h2><a class="ck-anchor" id="current"></a>Drug Safety Communications</h2><div class="table-responsive lcds-datatable lcds-datatable--ckeditor"><table class="table table-responsive table-striped" data-column-defs="[{ &quot;targets&quot;: 0, &quot;type&quot;: &quot;date&quot; }]" data-excel-button="true" data-order="[ 0, &quot;desc&quot; ]" data-paging="true" data-searching="true" summary="Drug Safety Communications" width="100%"><thead><tr><th style="width:15%;" scope="col">Date</th><th scope="col">Title</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>11-9-2026</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-requires-safety-labeling-changes-glucagon-peptide-1-receptor-agonists-glp-1-ras-due-potential" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="271f2fd1-0225-4579-94e9-cb14f06d5caf" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA Requires Safety Labeling Changes for Glucagon-Like Peptide-1 Receptor Agonists (GLP-1 RAs) Due to Potential Increased Risk of Rare But Serious Eye Condition">FDA Requires Safety Labeling Changes for Glucagon-Like Peptide-1 Receptor Agonists (GLP-1 RAs) Due to Potential Increased Risk of Rare But Serious Eye Condition</a></td></tr><tr><td>9-15-2026</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-approves-additional-information-labeling-kybella-deoxycholic-acid-injection-warning-adverse" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="8a20165d-8e3c-44c0-8589-3a8f70a25bfe" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA Approves Additional Information in Labeling for Kybella (Deoxycholic Acid) Injection Warning of Adverse Reactions Associated with Unapproved Use ">FDA Approves Additional Information in Labeling for Kybella (Deoxycholic Acid) Injection Warning of Adverse Reactions Associated with Unapproved Use</a></td></tr><tr><td>9-1-2026</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-adds-boxed-warning-labeling-ferric-carboxymaltose-injection-injectafer-describe-risk-low" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="cb9767c9-9d7f-4958-9878-d32b59a032c6" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA Adds Boxed Warning to Labeling for Ferric Carboxymaltose Injection (Injectafer) to Describe Risk of Low Phosphate Levels">FDA Adds Boxed Warning to Labeling for Ferric Carboxymaltose Injection (Injectafer) to Describe Risk of Low Phosphate Levels</a></td></tr><tr><td>6-10-2026</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-approves-labeling-changes-over-counter-otc-weight-loss-drug-alli-orlistat-warn-risk-kidney" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="3a4381b3-4b2a-4335-be8c-7e868efe07a5" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA Approves Labeling Changes for Over-the-Counter (OTC) Weight Loss Drug alli (Orlistat) to Warn of Risk of Kidney Stones and Kidney Injury    ">FDA Approves Labeling Changes for Over-the-Counter (OTC) Weight Loss Drug alli (Orlistat) to Warn of Risk of Kidney Stones and Kidney Injury</a></td></tr><tr><td>3-31-2026</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-identifies-cases-serious-liver-injury-patients-taking-tavneos-avacopan-severe-active-anti" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="0880d115-18d4-40a3-971a-49fc1824c6b5" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA Identifies Cases of Serious Liver Injury in Patients Taking Tavneos (avacopan) for Severe Active Anti-neutrophil Cytoplasmic Autoantibody (ANCA)-associated Vasculitis">FDA Identifies Cases of Serious Liver Injury in Patients Taking Tavneos (avacopan) for Severe Active Anti-neutrophil Cytoplasmic Autoantibody (ANCA)-associated Vasculitis</a></td></tr><tr><td>3-20-2026</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-requiring-warning-about-vitamin-b6-deficiency-and-associated-seizures-drug-products-containing" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="2c4b2b4b-7f43-4304-8475-0041993d9579" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA Is Requiring Warning about Vitamin B6 Deficiency and Associated Seizures for Drug Products Containing Carbidopa/Levodopa">FDA Is Requiring Warning about Vitamin B6 Deficiency and Associated Seizures for Drug Products Containing Carbidopa/Levodopa</a></td></tr><tr><td>1-13-2026</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-requests-removal-suicidal-behavior-and-ideation-warning-glucagon-peptide-1-receptor-agonist-glp" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="44e02b30-a2a2-4f54-9e58-e3d4026c652b" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA Requests Removal of Suicidal Behavior and Ideation Warning from Glucagon-Like Peptide-1 Receptor Agonist (GLP-1 RA) Medications">FDA Requests Removal of Suicidal Behavior and Ideation Warning from Glucagon-Like Peptide-1 Receptor Agonist (GLP-1 RA) Medications</a></td></tr><tr><td>8-28-2025</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-recommend-additional-earlier-mri-monitoring-patients-alzheimers-disease-taking-leqembi-lecanemab" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="f834f536-e33d-438d-9b1d-e89a1996ca31" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA to recommend additional, earlier MRI monitoring for patients with Alzheimer’s disease taking Leqembi (lecanemab)">FDA to recommend additional, earlier MRI monitoring for patients with Alzheimer’s disease taking Leqembi (lecanemab)</a></td></tr><tr><td>8-27-2025</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-removes-risk-evaluation-and-mitigation-strategy-rems-program-antipsychotic-drug-clozapine" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="eb904d07-2b13-4ad8-b326-667982a402d0" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA removes risk evaluation and mitigation strategy (REMS) program for the antipsychotic drug Clozapine">FDA removes risk evaluation and mitigation strategy (REMS) program for the antipsychotic drug Clozapine</a></td></tr><tr><td>7-31-2025</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-requiring-opioid-pain-medicine-manufacturers-update-prescribing-information-regarding-long-term" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="5bccb62c-279c-437d-86ed-70ebddac69e7" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA is requiring opioid pain medicine manufacturers to update prescribing information regarding long-term use">FDA is requiring opioid pain medicine manufacturers to update prescribing information regarding long-term use</a></td></tr><tr><td>6-30-2025</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-requires-expanded-labeling-about-weight-loss-risk-patients-younger-6-years-taking-extended" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="a1e9d3cd-3a88-49a4-baf1-028f81ee3d98" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA requires expanded labeling about weight loss risk in patients younger than 6 years taking extended-release stimulants for ADHD">FDA requires expanded labeling about weight loss risk in patients younger than 6 years taking extended-release stimulants for ADHD</a></td></tr><tr><td>6-18-2025</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-adds-warning-about-serious-risk-heat-related-complications-antinausea-patch-transderm-scop" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="ca1e546a-e1a8-4a4c-89d2-3af08204741d" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA adds warning about serious risk of heat-related complications with antinausea patch Transderm Scōp (scopolamine transdermal system)">FDA adds warning about serious risk of heat-related complications with antinausea patch Transderm Scōp (scopolamine transdermal system)</a></td></tr><tr><td>5-16-2025</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-requires-warning-about-rare-severe-itching-after-stopping-long-term-use-oral-allergy-medicines" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="083b823e-ec9c-4560-a85b-cc512ce271c8" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA requires warning about rare but severe itching after stopping long-term use of oral allergy medicines cetirizine or levocetirizine (Zyrtec, Xyzal, and other trade names)">FDA requires warning about rare but severe itching after stopping long-term use of oral allergy medicines cetirizine or levocetirizine (Zyrtec, Xyzal, and other trade names)</a></td></tr><tr><td>1-22-2025</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-adds-boxed-warning-about-rare-serious-allergic-reaction-called-anaphylaxis-multiple-sclerosis" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="7da8f083-5dbf-4d57-a7ca-7ae8184dda7f" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA adds Boxed Warning about a rare but serious allergic reaction called anaphylaxis with the multiple sclerosis medicine glatiramer acetate (Copaxone, Glatopa)">FDA adds Boxed Warning about a rare but serious allergic reaction called anaphylaxis with the multiple sclerosis medicine glatiramer acetate (Copaxone, Glatopa)</a></td></tr><tr><td>12-12-2024</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/serious-liver-injury-being-observed-patients-without-cirrhosis-taking-ocaliva-obeticholic-acid-treat" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="f70f5e7e-5109-49b5-a143-c8583bd5466d" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Serious liver injury being observed in patients without cirrhosis taking Ocaliva (obeticholic acid) to treat primary biliary cholangitis">Serious liver injury being observed in patients without cirrhosis taking Ocaliva (obeticholic acid) to treat primary biliary cholangitis</a></td></tr><tr><td>9-12-2024</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-adds-warning-about-rare-occurrence-serious-liver-injury-use-veozah-fezolinetant-hot-flashes-due" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="b47fdab6-8df9-4d7a-ab72-a279b70366f5" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA adds warning about rare occurrence of serious liver injury with use of Veozah (fezolinetant) for hot flashes due to menopause">FDA adds warning about rare occurrence of serious liver injury with use of Veozah (fezolinetant) for hot flashes due to menopause</a></td></tr><tr><td>1-19-2024</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-adds-boxed-warning-increased-risk-severe-hypocalcemia-patients-advanced-chronic-kidney-disease" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="451e716b-2bd2-4d0c-861a-6404d5161294" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA adds Boxed Warning for increased risk of severe hypocalcemia in patients with advanced chronic kidney disease taking osteoporosis medicine Prolia (denosumab)">FDA adds Boxed Warning for increased risk of severe hypocalcemia in patients with advanced chronic kidney disease taking osteoporosis medicine Prolia (denosumab)</a></td></tr><tr><td>1-11-2024</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/update-fdas-ongoing-evaluation-reports-suicidal-thoughts-or-actions-patients-taking-certain-type" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="210b6d04-73ad-4a15-ad19-8cd6da99383c" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Update on FDA’s ongoing evaluation of reports of suicidal thoughts or actions in patients taking a certain type of medicines approved for type 2 diabetes and obesity">Update on FDA’s ongoing evaluation of reports of suicidal thoughts or actions in patients taking a certain type of medicines approved for type 2 diabetes and obesity</a></td></tr><tr><td>11-28-2023</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-warns-rare-serious-drug-reaction-antiseizure-medicines-levetiracetam-keppra-keppra-xr-elepsia-xr" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="25772105-d48f-4c00-aabe-fa2c06d0838c" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA warns of rare but serious drug reaction to the antiseizure medicines levetiracetam (Keppra, Keppra XR, Elepsia XR, Spritam) and clobazam (Onfi, Sympazan) ">FDA warns of rare but serious drug reaction to the antiseizure medicines levetiracetam (Keppra, Keppra XR, Elepsia XR, Spritam) and clobazam (Onfi, Sympazan)</a></td></tr><tr><td>5-11-2023</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-updating-warnings-improve-safe-use-prescription-stimulants-used-treat-adhd-and-other-conditions" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="8e6f1681-8b65-4225-8271-5c76a1a9480e" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA updating warnings to improve safe use of prescription stimulants used to treat ADHD and other conditions">FDA updating warnings to improve safe use of prescription stimulants used to treat ADHD and other conditions</a></td></tr><tr><td>4-13-2023</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-updates-prescribing-information-all-opioid-pain-medicines-provide-additional-guidance-safe-use" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="6c07ade7-be7d-498d-980a-3743db52e6b9" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA updates prescribing information for all opioid pain medicines to provide additional guidance for safe use">FDA updates prescribing information for all opioid pain medicines to provide additional guidance for safe use</a></td></tr><tr><td>6-30-2022</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/fda-warns-about-possible-increased-risk-death-and-serious-side-effects-cancer-drug-copiktra" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="5576aa06-16b3-419a-a120-e2eb406eff7d" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA warns about possible increased risk of death and serious side effects with cancer drug Copiktra (duvelisib)">FDA warns about possible increased risk of death and serious side effects with cancer drug Copiktra (duvelisib)</a></td></tr><tr><td>6-1-2022</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/fda-approval-lymphoma-medicine-ukoniq-umbralisib-withdrawn-due-safety-concerns" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="95ba46f9-0b69-4d8a-b6b1-14b8df602724" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA approval of lymphoma medicine Ukoniq (umbralisib) is withdrawn due to safety concerns">FDA approval of lymphoma medicine Ukoniq (umbralisib) is withdrawn due to safety concerns</a></td></tr><tr><td>3-30-2022</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/fda-recommends-thyroid-monitoring-babies-and-young-children-who-receive-injections-iodine-containing" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="3600da26-bf66-4463-bc9f-c6c969e51da0" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA recommends thyroid monitoring in babies and young children who receive injections of iodine-containing contrast media for medical imaging">FDA recommends thyroid monitoring in babies and young children who receive injections of iodine-containing contrast media for medical imaging</a></td></tr><tr><td>2-3-2022</td><td><a href="/drugs/development-approval-process-drugs/fda-investigating-possible-increased-risk-death-lymphoma-medicine-ukoniq-umbralisib" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="b2ab1e95-ee7b-4f9c-9880-43e77e112a96" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA investigating possible increased risk of death with lymphoma medicine Ukoniq (umbralisib) ">FDA investigating possible increased risk of death with lymphoma medicine Ukoniq (umbralisib)</a></td></tr><tr><td>1-12-2022</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/fda-warns-about-dental-problems-buprenorphine-medicines-dissolved-mouth-treat-opioid-use-disorder" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="0e4a362c-2944-4433-a4a1-6eb726c35ef6" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA warns about dental problems with buprenorphine medicines dissolved in the mouth to treat opioid use disorder and pain ">FDA warns about dental problems with buprenorphine medicines dissolved in the mouth to treat opioid use disorder and pain</a></td></tr><tr><td>11-2-2021</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/fda-warns-getting-alcohol-based-hand-sanitizer-eyes-can-cause-serious-injury" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="964db521-4442-4d7a-93ae-3ad9546a4c02" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA warns that getting alcohol-based hand sanitizer in the eyes can cause serious injury ">FDA warns that getting alcohol-based hand sanitizer in the eyes can cause serious injury</a></td></tr><tr><td>9-1-21</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/fda-requires-warnings-about-increased-risk-serious-heart-related-events-cancer-blood-clots-and-death" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="4ec3359d-b7fe-41ca-9724-9602b68d8ca6" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA requires warnings about increased risk of serious heart-related events, cancer, blood clots, and death for JAK inhibitors that treat certain chronic inflammatory conditions">FDA requires warnings about increased risk of serious heart-related events, cancer, blood clots, and death for JAK inhibitors that treat certain chronic inflammatory conditions</a></td></tr><tr><td>7-20-2021</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/fda-requests-removal-strongest-warning-against-using-cholesterol-lowering-statins-during-pregnancy" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="68aa2469-6b1d-4aba-a2d0-3e399322d2a6" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA requests removal of strongest warning against using cholesterol-lowering statins during pregnancy; still advises most pregnant patients should stop taking statins">FDA requests removal of strongest warning against using cholesterol-lowering statins during pregnancy; still advises most pregnant patients should stop taking statins</a></td></tr><tr><td>6-16-2021</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/fda-warns-vapors-alcohol-based-hand-sanitizers-can-have-side-effects" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="0fc03d08-35bc-445c-ac70-4210b8b89453" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA warns that vapors from alcohol-based hand sanitizers can have side effects">FDA warns that vapors from alcohol-based hand sanitizers can have side effects</a></td></tr><tr><td>5-26-2021</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/due-risk-serious-liver-injury-fda-restricts-use-ocaliva-obeticholic-acid-primary-biliary-cholangitis" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="f22cf7f8-6fe4-49e9-be5d-2ed7f81706d9" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Due to risk of serious liver injury, FDA restricts use of Ocaliva (obeticholic acid) in primary biliary cholangitis (PBC) patients with advanced cirrhosis">Due to risk of serious liver injury, FDA restricts use of Ocaliva (obeticholic acid) in primary biliary cholangitis (PBC) patients with advanced cirrhosis</a></td></tr><tr><td>3-31-2021</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/studies-show-increased-risk-heart-rhythm-problems-seizure-and-mental-health-medicine-lamotrigine" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="19f8e082-1c53-466a-8814-d1f0185b2a18" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Studies show increased risk of heart rhythm problems with seizure and mental health medicine lamotrigine (Lamictal) in patients with heart disease">Studies show increased risk of heart rhythm problems with seizure and mental health medicine lamotrigine (Lamictal) in patients with heart disease</a></td></tr><tr><td>3-25-2021</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/fda-warns-abuse-and-misuse-nasal-decongestant-propylhexedrine-causes-serious-harm" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="c8c1514d-d31f-4cb3-9b91-de4423f0ec77" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA warns that abuse and misuse of the nasal decongestant propylhexedrine causes serious harm">FDA warns that abuse and misuse of the nasal decongestant propylhexedrine causes serious harm</a></td></tr><tr><td>2-4-2021</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/initial-safety-trial-results-find-increased-risk-serious-heart-related-problems-and-cancer-arthritis" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="760e4ace-aa81-4112-8779-efb5725411df" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Initial safety trial results find increased risk of serious heart-related problems and cancer with arthritis and ulcerative colitis medicine Xeljanz, Xeljanz XR (tofacitinib)">Initial safety trial results find increased risk of serious heart-related problems and cancer with arthritis and ulcerative colitis medicine Xeljanz, Xeljanz XR (tofacitinib)</a></td></tr><tr><td>10-15-2020</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/fda-recommends-avoiding-use-nsaids-pregnancy-20-weeks-or-later-because-they-can-result-low-amniotic" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="ffe6b059-007d-42e9-9bf4-798270296092" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA recommends avoiding use of NSAIDs in pregnancy at 20 weeks or later because they can result in low amniotic fluid">FDA recommends avoiding use of NSAIDs in pregnancy at 20 weeks or later because they can result in low amniotic fluid</a></td></tr><tr><td>9-24-2020</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/fda-warns-about-serious-problems-high-doses-allergy-medicine-diphenhydramine-benadryl" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="632f33bb-0019-49ef-adbb-d087413b3835" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA warns about serious problems with high doses of the allergy medicine diphenhydramine (Benadryl)">FDA warns about serious problems with high doses of the allergy medicine diphenhydramine (Benadryl)</a></td></tr><tr><td>9-23-2020</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/fda-requiring-boxed-warning-updated-improve-safe-use-benzodiazepine-drug-class" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="6601ed65-dcde-4d76-a52f-8a567978bb9a" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA  requiring Boxed Warning updated to improve safe use of benzodiazepine drug class">FDA requiring Boxed Warning updated to improve safe use of benzodiazepine drug class</a></td></tr><tr><td>8-26-2020</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/fda-removes-boxed-warning-about-risk-leg-and-foot-amputations-diabetes-medicine-canagliflozin" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="d53f0eaa-3628-4fd4-89c4-87429225380a" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA removes Boxed Warning about risk of leg and foot amputations for the diabetes medicine canagliflozin (Invokana, Invokamet, Invokamet XR)">FDA removes Boxed Warning about risk of leg and foot amputations for the diabetes medicine canagliflozin (Invokana, Invokamet, Invokamet XR)&nbsp;</a></td></tr><tr><td>7-23-2020</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-recommends-health-care-professionals-discuss-naloxone-all-patients-when-prescribing-opioid-pain" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="09442f78-edbc-42b3-996b-713b65ab6f39" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA recommends health care professionals discuss naloxone with all patients when prescribing opioid pain relievers or medicines to treat opioid use disorder ">FDA recommends health care professionals discuss naloxone with all patients when prescribing opioid pain relievers or medicines to treat opioid use disorder</a></td></tr><tr><td>4-24-2020</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-cautions-against-use-hydroxychloroquine-or-chloroquine-covid-19-outside-hospital-setting-or" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="bd524888-1b4f-4334-9410-e6b72f3dcbba" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA cautions against use of hydroxychloroquine or chloroquine for COVID-19 outside of the hospital setting or a clinical trial due to risk of heart rhythm problems">FDA cautions against use of hydroxychloroquine or chloroquine for COVID-19 outside of the hospital setting or a clinical trial due to risk of heart rhythm problems</a></td></tr><tr><td>3-4-2020</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-requires-boxed-warning-about-serious-mental-health-side-effects-asthma-and-allergy-drug" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="f1ac22c4-1d8a-47f8-8612-589abcf0bcf5" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA requires Boxed Warning about serious mental health side effects for asthma and allergy drug montelukast (Singulair); advises restricting use for allergic rhinitis">FDA requires Boxed Warning about serious mental health side effects for asthma and allergy drug montelukast (Singulair); advises restricting use for allergic rhinitis</a></td></tr><tr><td>2-13-2020</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-requests-withdrawal-weight-loss-drug-belviq-belviq-xr-lorcaserin-market" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="819211ec-fb39-45c9-9b55-653b470a0c30" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA requests the withdrawal of the weight-loss drug Belviq, Belviq XR (lorcaserin) from the market">FDA requests the withdrawal of the weight-loss drug Belviq, Belviq XR (lorcaserin) from the market&nbsp;</a></td></tr><tr><td>1-28-2020</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/fda-strengthens-warning-untreated-constipation-caused-schizophrenia-medicine-clozapine-clozaril-can" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="d92b723f-1f72-41bd-b505-a619e269d3b2" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="FDA strengthens warning that untreated constipation caused by schizophrenia medicine clozapine (Clozaril) can lead to serious bowel problems">FDA strengthens warning that untreated constipation caused by schizophrenia medicine clozapine (Clozaril) can lead to serious bowel problems</a></td></tr><tr><td>1-14-2020</td><td><a href="/drugs/drug-safety-communications/safety-clinical-trial-shows-possible-increased-risk-cancer-weight-loss-medicine-belviq-belviq-xr" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="af7af2e1-c69e-4cf4-9445-aeff36410247" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Safety clinical trial shows possible increased risk of cancer with weight-loss medicine Belviq, Belviq XR (lorcaserin)">Safety clinical trial shows possible increased risk of cancer with weight-loss medicine Belviq, Belviq XR (lorcaserin)</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><hr><h2>Resources&nbsp;</h2><ul><li>Full <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20260114214202/https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/drug-safety-communications">archived versions of Drug Safety Communications</a> published before 2020</li><li><a href="/drugs/development-approval-process-drugs" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="328c361f-31cd-4586-815a-9b7b9a83ac6e" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Development &amp; Approval Process | Drugs">Development &amp; Approval Process (Drugs)</a></li><li><a href="/drugs/development-approval-process-drugs/how-drugs-are-developed-and-approved" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="af94ef6c-09f7-4205-b0d0-9fd1e3f91e68" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="How Drugs are Developed and Approved">How Drugs are Developed and Approved</a></li><li><a href="/drugs/information-consumers-and-patients-drugs/fdas-drug-review-process-ensuring-drugs-are-safe-and-effective" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="d1961427-aa48-4b1f-8a7c-faf7b70754ac" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="The FDA's Drug Review Process: Ensuring Drugs Are Safe and Effective">FDA's Drug Review Process: Ensuring Drugs Are Safe and Effective</a></li><li><a href="/drugs/information-consumers-and-patients-drugs/think-it-through-managing-benefits-and-risks-medicines" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="93569200-878e-45f9-8d91-5d170aeab6aa" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Think It Through: Managing the Benefits and Risks of Medicines">Think It Through: Managing the Benefits and Risks of Medicines</a></li><li><a href="/drugs/information-consumers-and-patients-drugs/overview-our-role-regulating-and-approving-drugs-video-series" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="05b6c176-bda4-4548-8eb5-7d0dc99e0327" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Overview of our role regulating and approving drugs | Video series">Overview of our role regulating and approving drugs | Video series</a></li><li><a href="http://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cder/daf/index.cfm">Drugs@FDA: FDA-Approved Drugs</a></li><li><a href="/drugs/information-consumers-and-patients-drugs/find-information-about-drug" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="49890b97-a892-4c97-8f5e-81d94d794eac" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Find Information about a Drug">Find Information about a Drug</a></li></ul><br>

	
